483	    /// Drain the stream and deserialize the terminal assistant text into `T`.
484	    ///
485	    /// The terminal output is the concatenated text of the last
486	    /// [`AgentEvent::MessageOutput`]. On a correctly configured structured run
487	    /// the agent loop has already validated that text against `T`, so the parse
488	    /// here is expected to succeed; if it fails (e.g. `collect_typed` is called
489	    /// on a plain-text run), the parse error surfaces as [`AgentError::Other`].
490	    /// A failed run surfaces the underlying [`AgentError`]:
491	    /// structured-validation failures (carried by
492	    /// [`AgentEvent::StructuredOutputFailed`]) become
